DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("e^((x^2+3*x+5))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((10/(x))^4)^2-5*(((x^2))^(1/4))+4");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("([3, 11]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 11]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 11])");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{0, 1, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {0, 1, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {0, 1, 6})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-8, -7, 3, 6} U ({-8, -7, 3, 6}) U {-6, -4, 3, 4}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-8, -7, 3, 6} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -7, 3, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, -4, 3, 4})");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-6, -4, 3, 4} U {-8, -7, 3, 6}) U ({-6, -4, 3, 4} U {-6, -4, 3, 4}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, -4, 3, 4}) U {-6, -4, 3, 4}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`9+19-7-2`] is equal to [_____]{19}
---

What is the value of [`14/10+17/14`]? [_____]{2.61428571429}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-6, -4, 3, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, -7, 3, 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap B \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A \cup B) \cup (A \cup A) \cap A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{0, 1, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 11\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B) \cap B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, 5, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, 3, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<2, 5, 8>") . Compute("<-4, 3, -6>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<2, 5, 8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, 3, -6>") . Compute("<2, 5, 8>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, 3, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, 5, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, 5, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 0, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-2, 0, 1>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 5, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, 5, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 0, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, 5, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, 5, 7>") x Compute("<-2, 0, 1>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
